# Consumer rule (Cursor)

When the task is consuming knowledge material (courses, videos, audio, books,
PDFs, spreadsheets, slide decks, web pages, platform courses, email archives)
into a structured knowledge graph, querying such a graph, authoring courses
from consumed knowledge, or running bank connectors — use the consumer engine.

Resolve the engine first:
```bash
CONSUMER_HOME=""
for c in /Users/sharpe/consumer "$HOME/consumer" "tools/consumer"; do
  [ -d "$c" ] && CONSUMER_HOME="$c" && break
done
```

Front doors: `source.py <anything> --full` (chains ingest+graph),
`graph.py <mode> <query>` (six modes), `bank.py <list|status|consume|act>`,
`export.py --format json|jsonl|csv|md|sqlite|package`, `sync.py import-package`.
Local STT: transcribe.py. Full manual: skills/consumer/SKILL.md upstream.
